// VOLD_array_shrunk.schema — OLD: vals [4]int32
//
// One of the fixed form's UNLAWFUL lineage rows (docs/FIXED-FORM-VERSIONING-TESTS.md,
// internal/fixedunlawful). The OLD and the NEW file of this pair differ by
// EXACTLY [4]int32 -> [2]int32. `lead` and `trail` bracket the row's field.
//
// THIS PAIR IS DELIBERATELY UNLAWFUL: SPEC §5.1 refuses a narrowed bound ("bound narrowed (4 -> 2)"). A leg that
// lands min(4, 2) elements and drops the rest LOADS it.
// So the lineage entry is handed in by the probe and never read
// from a lock. The NEW reader must refuse old_array_shrunk.bin
// `layout_malformed` and write nothing (docs/FIXED-FORM-ALGORITHM.md §5.2, §5.4,
// §5.9 #30). Do not "fix" it.

package vold_array_shrunk

fixed table ArrayShrunk
{
    lead  uint32 = 1
    vals  [4]int32
    trail uint32 = 2
}
